part tsb_2
  tally 1
  law
  note "TSB-2 · The interest rate: ISB-R1-<yymm> in the first interest year (.1); later, the CPI-YY of the month two months before the month the interest year starts, less 100, plus ISB-MARGIN-<yymm>, never below 0, the index read as published on the interest year's first day (.2)."
  note "Gazette rows (GEN-6): a series' R1 and margin in one version governing its sale month, read at the purchase day (the households' def says at); a CPI-YY row governing the month it is for, known on its publication day, a flash estimate and the figure that replaced it each in its own version, so a read as known on the interest year's first day sees the one published by then. Only the series household D holds (ISB1901–ISB2405) and the CPI-YY months from 2019-11 are written."

source tsb_2 "Treasury Savings Bonds, terms of issue, TSB-2 The interest rate (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

index tsb2_month = month 2018-01..2064-12

input isb_r1[s in isb_series]: num question "What is this series' first-year rate, in % a year (ISB-R1, TSB-2 .1)?"

input isb_margin[s in isb_series]: num question "What is this series' margin, in % a year (ISB-MARGIN, TSB-2 .2)?"

input cpi_yy[m in tsb2_month]: num question "What is the CPI of this month, the same month a year before = 100 (CPI-YY, TSB-2 .2)?"

input tsb2_lag: int question "How many months before the interest year's first month is the CPI read (TSB-2 .2)?"

version tsb2_v1
  cite tsb_2
  governs 2018-01-01..
  known 2017-11-20
  enters 2018-01-01
  note "TSB-2 v1, in force 2018-01-01 until replaced, published 2017-11-20; governs series issued from January 2018."
  tsb2_lag = 2 "TSB-2 v1 .2: the month two months before"

